    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18586" root="سأل" body-key="s">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُؤَالٌ</span></b>  an inf. n. of 1. (S, M, K, &amp;c.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  [It is
often used as a subst. properly so called; like
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَسْأَلَةٌ</span>; meaning <i>A question; an interrogation;</i>
correlative of <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَوَابٌ</span>: and <i>a demand,</i> or <i>petition:</i>
and as such has a pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">سُؤَالَاتٌ</span>; perhaps postclassical.]

